(7196338, 1107283, 63218, '<td valign="top">WOW! I love what you did with this. The color &amp; curving lines &amp; shapes are seductive. Interesting that the cloud shadows don''t show up as much in fullsize as they do in thumbnail. The cloud shadows do a lot to make this interesting, but in a subtle way. I like it.</td>', 'WOW! I love what you did with this. The color & curving lines & shapes are seductive. Interesting that the cloud shadows don''t show up as much in fullsize as they do in thumbnail. The cloud shadows do a lot to make this interesting, but in a subtle way. I like it.', '2014-03-31 11:35:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(7196370, 1106981, 59029, '<td valign="top">uhm there is not meant to be any sky in the pic...please read challenge description.</td>', 'uhm there is not meant to be any sky in the pic...please read challenge description.', '2014-03-31 12:30:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(7196390, 1107347, 12611, '<td valign="top">First off, I like the use of warm ground in front of cool trees. Secondly, I often stand and stare at the edge of a forest, with trees like sentinels, holding things out- or keeping things in?</td>', 'First off, I like the use of warm ground in front of cool trees. Secondly, I often stand and stare at the edge of a forest, with trees like sentinels, holding things out- or keeping things in?', '2014-03-31 12:50:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(7196391, 1107430, 12611, '<td valign="top">The cloud dappling enhances the shot, almost an abstract,</td>', 'The cloud dappling enhances the shot, almost an abstract,', '2014-03-31 12:51:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(7196397, 1107462, 30861, '<td valign="top">WOW. Fascinating image. If I''d been standing ON earth these clouds would have been part of "sky" for sure. Being ABOVE earth and looking down, do they become OF earth? What if the ground view were mostly clear, with a few clouds drifing along between you and the ground?<br/> <br/>I''d love to see a debate on this in the forums, after voting, if you don''t mind. Feel free to PM me, I''m done voting.</td>', 'WOW. Fascinating image. If I''d been standing ON earth these clouds would have been part of "sky" for sure. Being ABOVE earth and looking down, do they become OF earth? What if the ground view were mostly clear, with a few clouds drifing along between you and the ground? I''d love to see a debate on this in the forums, after voting, if you don''t mind. Feel free to PM me, I''m done voting.', '2014-03-31 13:27:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(7196398, 1107525, 30861, '<td valign="top">mud-luscious!</td>', 'mud-luscious!', '2014-03-31 13:28:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(7196400, 1107235, 30861, '<td valign="top">Pity about the halo on the bird. I can show you how to fix it lickety-split, if that would be helpful; or did you just not notice? Great shot, wonderful how we have a bird in flight but no sky. 8</td>', 'Pity about the halo on the bird. I can show you how to fix it lickety-split, if that would be helpful; or did you just not notice? Great shot, wonderful how we have a bird in flight but no sky. 8', '2014-03-31 13:33:24.000000', NULL, 1),
